                "headline": "Flash Flood Warning issued September 14 at 3:23PM MST until September 14 at 5:00PM MST by NWS Tucson AZ",
                "description": "At 323 PM MST, Doppler radar indicated thunderstorms producing heavy\nrain across the warned area. Between 0.6 and 1.1 inches of rain have\nfallen. Flash flooding is ongoing or expected to begin shortly.\n\nHAZARD...Flash flooding caused by thunderstorms.\n\nSOURCE...Radar indicated.\n\nIMPACT...Flash flooding of small creeks and streams, urban areas,\nhighways, streets and underpasses as well as other poor\ndrainage and low-lying areas.\n\nSome locations that will experience flash flooding include...\nWhetstone, Huachuca City and Fairbank.\n\nThis includes the following highways...\nRoute 90 between mile markers 309 and 313. Route 82 between mile\nmarkers 52 and 61.",
                "instruction": "Turn around, don't drown when encountering flooded roads. Most flood\ndeaths occur in vehicles.\n\nBe aware of your surroundings and do not drive on flooded roads.",
